{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The platform's own record establishes the deviation the rider complains of: trip_record.actual_distance_km is 8.3 km against trip_record.optimal_distance_km of 7.3 km, a deviation of 1.00 km under POL-RD-22's subtraction, and the recommended route ran via Seletar Road while the vehicle went by Yio Chu Kang Road and Jalan Kayu. The rider's account - 'at least 1 km more' - is therefore not an assertion that needs corroboration from elsewhere; it is the platform's own figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05007", "EV-GPS-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's counterstatement that the distance was 'about the same' is contradicted by the record it comes from. The trip record logs a route_deviation_detected at Yishun Avenue 1 / Yio Chu Kang Road and a route_rejoined at Sengkang West Avenue / Jalan Kayu, and the GPS trace runs on Yio Chu Kang Road and Jalan Kayu from 13:27:45 to 13:35:45, on a route the record itself describes as recommended via Seletar Road. The deviation is a recorded fact of this trip, not a matter of the rider's impression.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05007", "EV-TRIP-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.last_fix_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no traffic justification for leaving the recommended route. The LTA traffic artifact covering the recommended segment - Seletar Road, Yishun Avenue 1 to Sengkang West Avenue, both directions, valid 12:51 to 14:21 and so overlapping the trip window - records no incident, roadwork or closure, with speed bands 5-6, and the derived result is justifies_reroute false with type NONE; the artifact is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 and was retrieved by the platform rather than supplied by a party. POL-RD-23 makes congestion, an incident or a closure the only justifications, and it says in terms that a driver's assertion with no such data does not justify a reroute - which is all the driver offers here ('Jalan Kayu road is smoother'). Rows (a), (b) and (c) of POL-RD-24 are therefore unavailable to the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05007-01", "EV-TRIP-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "traffic_advisory.derived.v7.justifies_reroute",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver also never told the rider he was leaving the recommended route. The chat log for this trip carries 0 messages and the trip record lists no in-app calls, and no call recording is in the record at all. POL-RD-21 requires notice by in-app chat before or at the point of deviation - a brief reason is enough, but something is required - and a verbal notice with no recording cannot be established. Nothing in this record shows the rider agreed to the longer route, so the 'rider informed and agreed' limb of POL-RD-24 never opens and the rider's objection stands unaddressed by the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05007", "EV-TRIP-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.message_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider paid for the extra kilometre rather than merely observing it: the trip was metered on distance, with distance_charged_km of 8.3 at the 0.72 SGD per-km rate producing a distance fare of 5.98 SGD inside the 12.65 SGD total, while the recommended route was 7.3 km. The disputed sum is the excess distance the deviation added to the meter, and the rider's claim is directed at exactly that.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05007", "EV-TRIP-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the deviation is found to be over the 1.0 km tolerance, POL-RD-24(d) applies and the excess distance fare is refunded in full: the deviation distance times fare_breakdown.per_km_rate_sgd, without surge, 1.00 x 0.72 = 0.72 SGD. That 0.72 SGD, not the 2.50 SGD named in the claim, is the clause's own measure of the excess, and under POL-GEN-03 a partial refund is read against the filing party - here the rider - so it is the rider and not the driver who stops carrying that charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05007", "EV-TRIP-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not ask the judge to re-measure the route; he asks that the outcome not be inferred from the very edge of a tolerance. The deviation the record yields is 1.00 km - the difference of two figures the trip record states only to one decimal place, 7.3 and 8.3 - and it sits exactly on POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance, so whether POL-RD-24(d) or (e) governs depends on a boundary the record's own precision does not resolve. That is the situation POL-GEN-26 addresses: where the fact a rule needs cannot be established, the case is escalated with the open question stated rather than decided on the edge of tolerance. On escalation no money issues and the amount is held rather than collected, so the rider is not left carrying the disputed charge while a human reviews which side of the tolerance this trip fell on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05007", "EV-GPS-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-RD-22", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.within_tolerance",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
